NOTICE — `changi::puff`
=======================

`src/puff/` contains a Rust port of the R package `puff` (MIT). See
`LICENSE.puff` for the upstream licence and the relicensing note.

Upstream
--------

    Project  : puff — Simulate and Visualize the Gaussian Puff Forward
               Atmospheric Model
    URL      : https://github.com/Hammerling-Research-Group/puff
    CRAN     : https://cran.r-project.org/package=puff
    Version  : 0.1.1
    Commit   : 5213d58daad5b6a2837890ff5da20b9b2c4e8213
    Licence  : MIT + file LICENSE
    Copyright: 2025 Hammerling Research Group

Upstream authors, as listed in `DESCRIPTION`:

    Teagan Ward, Philip Waggoner, Will Daniels, Meng Jia,
    Dorit Hammerling (thesis supervisor), Callan Okenberg (maintainer)
    — Colorado School of Mines

Underlying model reference:

    Jia, M., Fish, R., Daniels, W., Sprinkle, B. and Hammerling, D. (2024).
    doi:10.26434/chemrxiv-2023-hc95q-v3

This is an independent fork. It is **not** affiliated with, endorsed by, or
supported by the Hammerling Research Group or the Colorado School of Mines.
Defects in this port are this project's, not theirs.

What was ported, and what was not
---------------------------------

Ported (upstream's physics, 1 219 of 2 296 R lines):

    R/helpers.R              -> src/puff/{stability,dispersion,wind,concentration}.rs
    R/simulate_sensor_mode.R -> src/puff/simulate.rs
    R/simulate_grid_mode.R   -> src/puff/simulate.rs

Not ported:

    R/plots.R (1 077 lines, 47% of the package) — ggplot2/plotly chart
    construction with no physics. `changi` is a headless library that must
    build for Android and wasm32, and does not own its caller's plotting.

Deviations from upstream are documented in `docs/puff-code-to-code.md` and
flagged at each call site in the source. The one place the port's DEFAULT
differs is the emission policy: upstream's data-frame recycling doubles the
emitted mass whenever the stability class is ambiguous, and this port defaults
to the mass-conserving reading while offering the upstream behaviour by name.

Verification
------------

The port is verified code-to-code against the upstream R at commit 5213d58 —
10 182 reference cases produced by executing upstream itself, replayed through
the port by `tests/puff_code_to_code.rs`. Results in
`docs/puff-code-to-code.md`. That is verification, not validation: it shows the
translation is faithful, not that the model reproduces measured dispersion.
